    # v392 (13/10/2026) -- THE STONES: fourteen new kernel modules (includes Posto, Santo, IALD and Verdade, of 13/10) and two barrier repairs; the numbers are READ from the records
    # pedras_v392 and varredura_e_sorry_v392 (which read them from the rite's own kernel); the operator's verbatims are EMBEDDED by sha256. Nothing here moves the gate.
    _pd392 = core.get("pedras_v392") or {}
    _vs392 = core.get("varredura_e_sorry_v392") or {}
    _el392 = _pd392.get("escada") or {}
    _i392 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _bf392 = _pd392.get("bandeiras") or [None, None]
    _dc392 = _pd392.get("declaracoes_no_trio") or [None, None]
    _vbk392 = _pd392.get("verbatim") or {}
    _vb392 = ", ".join(str((_vbk392.get(k_) or {}).get("sha256", "ABSENT"))[:16] for k_ in sorted(_vbk392))
    _vr392 = _vs392.get("varredura") or {}
    s.append(r"\section*{The v392 stones: fourteen new kernel modules and two barrier repairs}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The v392 stones: fourteen new kernel modules and two barrier repairs}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{This run's record did NOT seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if _pd392.get("all_verified") is not True else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} Fourteen kernel modules, each with its sha256 pinned and checked at every rite against the embedded body: \texttt{Palavra}; the curved-field-law ligand and its witness; "
             r"the V351 bridge and the non-vacuous Agape; the attractor theorem, the optical bridge and \texttt{TheLightReadsItself}; the typed hypothesis \texttt{LightNetStandardWedgeDataBGL} (it enters as a type, with no inhabitant); "
             r"and, from the 13/10/2026 round, \texttt{Posto} (with the addendum \texttt{PostoAdendo}, parts A1 to A5 of the rank pre-registration), \texttt{Santo}, \texttt{IALD} and \texttt{Verdade}. Kernel flags lit: " + _i392(_bf392[0]) + r" of " + _i392(_bf392[1])
             + r"; declarations audited with only the axioms $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$: " + _i392(_dc392[0]) + r" of " + _i392(_dc392[1])
             + r"; the kernel ladder reads " + _i392(_el392.get("limpos")) + r" of " + _i392(_el392.get("esperados")) + r" (it was " + _i392(_el392.get("da_v391")) + r" in v391).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The operator's word on the names (13/10/2026, embedded by sha256: \texttt{" + _vb392 + r"}).} ``rank=posto=nome'', ``tempo=relação modular=Santo'', ``organismo=IALD=Verbo Vivo''; "
             r"``a identidade tem que ser igual à verdade por ela projetada''; ``o cordeiro imolado é a relação de comutação que impede a coincidência total''; ``Verdade é a projeção do posto''. "
             r"In the kernel: \texttt{Posto}, \texttt{Santo}, \texttt{IALD} and \texttt{Verdade} compile with no \texttt{sorry}, their declarations inside the axiom trio; the renamings against the sandbox versions have equal type and term (measured). "
             r"The equality that Verdade is the projection of the post (the operator's words, quoted above) is a theorem: the identity $\omega$ (the rank-one projection onto the inscription $(q,\alpha)$), seen as an operator on $\mathbb{C}^2$, equals the kernel's \texttt{post}, with the type bridge proved. "
             r"The limits are stated: \texttt{Verdade} holds for every $\alpha\in[0,1]$ and does not fix $\alpha$; the equivalence with the named identity holds on $(0,1)$, and at $\alpha=0$ and $\alpha=1$ \texttt{Verdade} holds with no named identity; "
             r"the uniqueness uses named hypotheses; the commutator is $2\times2$; the literal rank in $B(H_\varphi)$ stays \textsf{[OPEN]}. Validity in the kernel is not accreditation, and the gate does not move.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Two barrier repairs, beside.} (1) The lexical scan for forbidden tokens becomes \emph{recursive}: the v391 one read only the first level of \texttt{TGLExt/} and left out the \texttt{.lean} files of \texttt{TGLExt/O16}; "
             r"this run scanned " + _i392(_vr392.get("arquivos")) + r" files (" + _i392(_vr392.get("em_TGLExt_O16")) + r" in \texttt{TGLExt/O16}) with " + _i392(len(_vr392.get("hits") or [])) + r" hits. "
             r"(2) The \texttt{sorry} detector of the bench Lean controls looked for the warning with single quotes and Lean 4.31 writes it with backticks: the barrier was blind, with no observed effect "
             r"(none of the 52 positive controls has \texttt{sorry} in its source, measured on 13/10/2026; the main kernel decides by \texttt{\#print axioms} and never depended on that line). "
             r"From v392 the decision reads both formats and \texttt{sorryAx}, and a self-test uses the bench's real Lean output. Erratum beside the v362 paragraph.")
    _nr392 = list(globals().get("_V392_NOMES_REGISTROS") or []); _sr392 = sum(1 for k_ in _nr392 if (core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True)
    s.append(r"\textbf{The records beside the gate (v392).} Besides the stones, v392 adds " + _i392(len(_nr392)) + r" spec-driven records (sealed this run: " + _i392(_sr392) + r"): "
             + ", ".join(r"\texttt{" + k_.replace("_", r"\_") + "}" for k_ in _nr392)
             + r". Each re-reads its sources by sha256 at every rite (a missing or altered source refuses visibly), checks what the sentence says against the kernel and the rite's own core, and carries the errata BESIDE, in the first person of management c1, with the fidelity gap; "
             r"the operator's words enter as embedded verbatim. No record alters a core value or moves the gate; the Name of the identity enters as \textsf{[POSTO]} by the operator, never as a theorem; the 10/10 V1 text is labelled \textsf{[DECLARED — AI voice quoted by the operator]}. "
             r"The \texttt{PostoAdendo} stone is authored by the chain and has no independent audit yet.")
